dialect grammar
grammar deflate.diff
extension zz
start document
comment none

# P2-FG2: real one-line `DiffCodec::print_diff`/`parse_diff` shape ALREADY emitted by
# `../../🦀️.rs`'s `print_deflate_diff`/`parse_deflate_diff` (hand-rolled -- `dict_id:
# Option<Option<u32>>` is a tri-state field, `dsl_derive::classify_field` peels exactly one
# `Option<..>` layer before binding and no `impl<T: DslField> DslField for Option<T>` exists
# anywhere in the `dsl` crate, so `#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]` is not usable here -- same blocker
# `XmlDiff`/`GifDiff` hit, confirmed via real `cargo check` per that file's own doc comment).
# Every keyword/tag token below is copied verbatim from the real `format!(...)` call sites, not
# invented. `comment none`: not strictly required by any token this grammar's own alphabet
# produces (hex payloads are lowercase-only, never containing `#`), kept for consistency with the
# sibling ../../📸️snapshot/📝️text grammar and because a `#` appearing in future demo/fixture
# growth should fail loudly as a real parse mismatch, not silently vanish as a comment.
#
# `hex` (bare `hex`, referenced below but deliberately NOT defined as a production in this file)
# is the framework's built-in `hex` MACRO -- see the mandatory-macro rationale in
# `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §1.3(f)/§3 pitfall 2. Safe here even greedily: `payload-tok` is always
# the LAST token in `document`'s sequence, so there is no following bareword literal for `hex`'s
# own `Star`-less, largest-span-first macro match to swallow.
document = compression-method-tok? window-bits-tok? level-tok? dict-id-tok? payload-tok?

compression-method-tok = "compression-method" "=" INT
window-bits-tok = "window-bits" "=" INT

# `enc_level_hint`/`dec_level_hint` -- single-letter tag (`f`/`a`/`d`/`m`), a DIFFERENT
# convention from the mutations facet's own bare kebab-case `DeflateLevelHint` tags (this diff
# codec's own local grammar choice, `GifDisposal`'s `enc_disposal` precedent per the Rust doc
# comment on `HandcraftedDiffCodec` in `../../🦀️.rs`).
level-tok = "level" "=" level-lit
level-lit = "f" | "a" | "d" | "m"

# `encode_option`'s uniform tri-state shape (`📖️grammar-recipe.md` §1.4): `[0]`
# (unchanged/None) / `[1,<value>]` (Some) -- `dict_id`'s OWN `Option<Option<u32>>` tri-state,
# distinct from the plain-optional "field changed at all" wrapper every OTHER token here uses
# (a token's mere PRESENCE on the line already means "field changed"; only `dict_id` needs a
# second layer to distinguish "cleared" from "set").
dict-id-tok = "dict-id" "=" opt-int
opt-int = "[" "0" "]" | "[" "1" "," INT "]"

# `payload`'s own `Option<Vec<u8>>` is the DIFF's plain "field changed at all" wrapper (NOT a
# second tri-state -- `DeflateSnapshot::payload` itself is a bare, never-nullable `Vec<u8>`), so
# its token is only present when the field changed, and its value is always lowercase hex, never
# itself optional -- matches `hex_encode`'s own local grammar idiom (same reasoning
# `DeflateSnapshot`'s own ../../📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs `ArtifactDsl` impl gives for using hex
# instead of base64 at THIS grammar layer: no external dependency, no escaping needed).
payload-tok = "payload" "=" hex
